{"title":"Product Designer-Developer Roadmap","role":"Product Designer-Developer","summary":"A Product Designer-Developer combines UX/UI design, product thinking, frontend engineering, and software development to design and build digital products.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Computer Science & Design (CSD)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Product Designer-Developer combines UX/UI design, product thinking, frontend engineering, and software development to design and build digital products."},{"type":"p","text":"Unlike a traditional UI designer who may focus primarily on visual design, or a frontend developer who primarily implements designs, this role operates across the product lifecycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User problem","Research","UX","UI","Prototype","Frontend","API integration","Testing","Product iteration"]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX/UI design"},{"text":"Human-computer interaction"},{"text":"Product thinking"},{"text":"Frontend development"},{"text":"Design systems"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"APIs"},{"text":"Databases"},{"text":"AI-powered product development"},{"text":"Analytics"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Product Designer-Developer can specialize in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product Design"},{"text":"UX Engineering"},{"text":"Frontend Engineering"},{"text":"Design Engineering"},{"text":"UX/UI Development"},{"text":"Design Systems Engineering"},{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"AI Product Design"},{"text":"Developer Experience (DevEx)"},{"text":"Design Technologist"},{"text":"Product Engineering"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Long-term progression can lead toward Senior Product Designer, Design Engineer, Product Engineer, UX Engineering Lead, Product Manager, Design Systems Lead, or Product Design/Engineering Manager."}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Programming + Design Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build both technical and visual foundations."},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"JavaScript"},{"text":"HTML"},{"text":"CSS"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Basic problem solving"},{"text":"JavaScript should become the primary programming language for product development."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Visual hierarchy"},{"text":"Typography"},{"text":"Color theory"},{"text":"Layout"},{"text":"Spacing"},{"text":"Grids"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Responsive design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"FigJam"},{"text":"GitHub"},{"text":"VS Code"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — UX + Frontend Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop two parallel capabilities."},{"type":"h","text":"UX"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User research"},{"text":"User personas"},{"text":"User journeys"},{"text":"Information architecture"},{"text":"User flows"},{"text":"Wireframing"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Usability testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Frontend"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HTML5"},{"text":"CSS3"},{"text":"JavaScript"},{"text":"DOM"},{"text":"Responsive design"},{"text":"Flexbox"},{"text":"CSS Grid"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Browser fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then move into:"},{"type":"h","text":"React.js"}]},{"heading":"User Research & Product Discovery","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A good product designer-developer should understand why a product needs to exist, not only how it looks."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":